    ('20367', 7, $$Marilize has finished her drawing$$),
    ('20367', 8, $$Next went Kuda$$),
    ('20367', 9, $$Kuda has finished his drawing$$),
    ('20367', 10, $$The bell finally rings for the pupils to go home.$$),
    ('20367', 11, $$Did you enjoy your last holiday?$$),
    ('20550', 0, $$A little girl was sent by their parents to her grandfather who has lived behind the forest she went herself with happiness.$$),
    ('20550', 1, $$When she reached near the forest she met with a careless goat and talked to her to go carefully because there is a meeting of animals in the forest.$$),
    ('20550', 2, $$When she reached in the middle of the forest, she found many animal near the way and she run and run and making noise.$$),
    ('20550', 3, $$When she went out of the forest she met also many birds together making noise. The little girl run and making more noise. Her grandfather heard her.$$),
    ('20550', 4, $$Her grandfather talked to her wife that is their granddaughter. He went to see her quickly with his dog and find her tired.$$),
    ('20550', 5, $$When they reached at home she entered and greet other children then she took food. After eating she talked about what happened across the way.$$),
    ('20550', 6, $$After telling what happened and getting advice of not passing in the forest without another one she went happily to play with other children.$$),
    ('20550', 7, $$She didn't pass again in the forest without anyone.$$),
    ('20587', 0, $$One day, the hyena's son died.$$),
    ('20587', 1, $$A donkey heard the news.$$),
    ('20587', 2, $$One old donkey said, "Brothers, we must go to the hyena's funeral and show respect. "$$),
    ('20587', 3, $$"Listen," said the old donkey. "If we don't go, the hyenas will be angry with us. They will have a reason to eat us. "$$),
    ('20587', 4, $$The hyenas saw the donkeys outside their house.$$),
    ('20587', 5, $$This was the donkeys’ song:$$),
    ('20587', 6, $$The dead hyena's uncle answered them with another song: "Your song is good. Your words are sweet. Come in, dear donkeys. Take a seat! "$$),
    ('20587', 7, $$The donkeys were very frightened now.$$),
    ('20587', 8, $$The oldest donkey said, "My lords, we came to show respect to you. We are sorry that your son is dead. We will pray to God to comfort you. Now we must go back to our home. "$$),
    ('20587', 9, $$The donkeys began to go.$$),
    ('20587', 10, $$The donkeys looked at each other.$$),
    ('20587', 11, $$The hyenas cut off the donkeys' lips, and ate them.$$),
    ('20587', 12, $$Again, the donkeys tried to go.$$),
    ('20587', 13, $$"Stop! " Cried the dead hyena's uncle. "My brothers, will you let these donkeys go? Look at them! We can see their teeth! They are laughing at us! "$$),
    ('20587', 14, $$They jumped on the donkeys. They killed them, and began to eat them.$$),
    ('20587', 15, $$Before the oldest donkey died, he looked at the hyenas and said, "Wicked hyenas, we came with our song to comfort you but we were wrong! Next time you are hungry, don't pretend that you need a reason to eat your friend! "$$),
    ('20814', 0, $$Nusha was a little girl who wasn't very good at anything.$$),
    ('20814', 1, $$But when she was 12, she found she could fly.$$),
    ('20814', 2, $$She flew to school when she was late.$$),
    ('20814', 3, $$She flew to her grandma's house on weekends.$$),
    ('20814', 4, $$She flew to the market because it was quicker.$$),
    ('20814', 5, $$She flew across the sea to church.$$),
    ('20814', 6, $$She flew along the beach and saw people kissing.$$),
    ('20814', 7, $$She flew up to get coconuts from trees.$$),
    ('20814', 8, $$People paid her to help fix their roofs.$$),
    ('20814', 9, $$All her friends asked her how she did it.$$),
    ('20814', 10, $$"You have to think very, very hard," she said, "and you have to really really want to do it. "$$),
    ('20814', 11, $$One day she met a boy who could fly too.$$),
    ('20814', 12, $$They started to go out together.$$),
    ('20814', 13, $$Maybe they got married and had children in the end.$$),
    ('2084', 0, $$Once upon a time, Hen and Eagle were friends. They lived in peace with all the other birds. None of them could fly.$$),
    ('2084', 1, $$One day, there was famine in the land. Eagle had to walk very far to find food. She came back very tired. "There must be an easier way to travel! " said Eagle.$$),
    ('2084', 2, $$After a good night's sleep, Hen had a brilliant idea. She began collecting the fallen feathers from all their bird friends. "Let's sew them together on top of our own feathers," she said. "Perhaps that will make it easier to travel. "$$),
    ('2084', 3, $$Eagle was the only one in the village with a needle, so she started sewing first. She made herself a pair of beautiful wings and flew high above Hen. Hen borrowed the needle but she soon got tired of sewing. She left the needle on the cupboard and went into the kitchen to prepare food for her children.$$),
    ('2084', 4, $$But the other birds had seen Eagle flying away. They asked Hen to lend them the needle to make wings for themselves too. Soon there were birds flying all over the sky.$$),
    ('2084', 5, $$When the last bird returned the borrowed needle, Hen was not there. So her children took the needle and started playing with it. When they got tired of the game, they left the needle in the sand.$$),
    ('2084', 6, $$Later that afternoon, Eagle returned. She asked for the needle to fix some feathers that had loosened on her journey. Hen looked on the cupboard. She looked in the kitchen. She looked in the yard. But the needle was nowhere to be found.$$),
    ('2084', 7, $$"Just give me a day," Hen begged Eagle. "Then you can fix your wing and fly away to get food again. " "Just one more day," said Eagle. "If you can't find the needle, you'll have to give me one of your chicks as payment. "$$),
    ('2084', 8, $$When Eagle came the next day, she found Hen scratching in the sand, but no needle. So Eagle flew down very fast and caught one of the chicks. She carried it away. Forever after that, whenever Eagle appears, she finds Hen scratching in the sand for the needle.$$),
    ('2084', 9, $$As the shadow of Eagle's wing falls on the ground, Hen warns her chicks. "Get out of the bare and dry land. " And they respond: "We are not fools. We will run. "$$),
    ('20853', 0, $$There was once an old woman living by herself inside a bottle. She complained all the time.$$),
    ('20853', 1, $$One day a fairy passed by her home and saw her looking very sad.$$),
    ('20853', 2, $$The fairy stopped and asked her, "What is the problem? Why are you so sad? "$$),
    ('20853', 3, $$"I am tired of living in a bottle," replied the old lady.$$),
    ('20853', 4, $$The fairy said to her, "Stand up, clap your hands twice, and turn around three times. "$$),
    ('20853', 5, $$After doing what she was told to do, the old woman found herself in a small house.$$),
    ('20853', 6, $$After a few days the fairy came back and found the woman still unhappy.$$),
    ('20853', 7, $$The fairy asked her, "What is wrong now? Why are you sad? "$$),
    ('20853', 8, $$"This house is too small. I do not like it," responded the old woman.$$),
    ('20853', 9, $$The fairy said to her, "Stand up, clap your hands twice, and turn around three times. "$$),
    ('20853', 10, $$After doing what she was told to do, the old woman found herself in a big house.$$),
    ('20853', 11, $$The fairy came to see the old woman again. She found her still unhappy and grumpy.$$),
    ('20853', 12, $$The fairy asked her, "What is wrong old lady? " The old lady responded, "This house is dark and dirty. "$$),
    ('20853', 13, $$The fairy said to her, "Stand up, clap your hands twice, and turn around three times. "$$),
    ('20853', 14, $$After doing what she was told to do, the old woman found herself back inside the bottle.$$),
    ('20853', 15, $$The old woman could not see the blessings she received. She ended up in her bottle, alone and unhappy.$$),
    ('20870', 0, $$Ostrich and Lioness were once good friends.$$),
